# Project-specific
*.autosave.json

# Editor-generated artifacts (sessions, exports, scratch meshes).
# The session pattern is intentionally narrow — matching the
# YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS prefix the editor writes — so that example /
# documentation JSONs (e.g. ``01_demo.json``) are not silently
# excluded.  Add a literal filename here (or ``geo_paths_*.txt``
# style) if a new artifact category is introduced.
#
# ``*.txt`` used to be listed bare.  It has exactly one producer —
# ``geo_shoot._on_export_paths`` writes ``geo_paths_<timestamp>.txt`` —
# so the broad form bought nothing and silently swallowed every other
# text file, ``requirements.txt`` included (that one survives only
# because it was committed before the rule existed, and a
# ``git rm --cached`` + re-add would have lost it).
geo_paths_*.txt
#
# ``*.vtk`` deliberately stays broad: the editor's ``v`` export and the
# CLI's ``--vtk`` both derive their filename from the loaded session
# stem (``<stem>_NN.vtk``), which is arbitrary, so no narrow pattern
# can cover them.  A reference mesh you *do* want tracked therefore
# needs an explicit ``git add -f``.
*.vtk
20[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.json

# Claude Code workspace metadata
.claude/
